<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.9.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02228</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.9.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>113acb34-1664-4f64-9cd6-95e4cc0c8d97</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><emphasis><emphasis>
    <para>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</para>
  </emphasis></emphasis>
<para>For questions 1 – 5, solve each quadratic equation by rewriting it in factored form and using the zero product property.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2 + 11x + 35 = 7\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = -4\) and \(x = -7\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -6\) and \(x = -7\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 14\) and \(x = -3\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -5\) and \(x = -7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -4\) and \(x = -7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2− 14x + 20 = -25\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = 3\) and \(x = 15\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 10\) and \(x = 2\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -10\) and \(x = -4\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 9\) and \(x = 5\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = 9\) and \(x = 5\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2− 6x − 52 = -12\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = -16\) and \(x = 10\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 8\) and \(x = -8\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 10\) and \(x = -4\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -8\) and \(x = 5\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = 10\) and \(x = -4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2 − x − 64 = -8\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = 8\) and \(x = -8\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -7\) and \(x = 8\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 28\) and \(x = -2\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 4\) and \(x = -14\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -7\) and \(x = 8\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2 + 9x + 13 = -5\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = -3\) and \(x = -6\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -9\) and \(x = -2\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 8\) and \(x = 1\) </item>
  <item> \(x = 3\) and \(x = 6\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x = -3\) and \(x = -6\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Without graphing, identify the function whose graph has only one zero.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 9\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 13x + 42\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 8x + 16\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2 − 8x + 16\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Without graphing, identify the function whose graph has only one zero.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2+ 7x − 30\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2+ x − 30\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2+ 12x + 36\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2+ 12x + 36\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Without graphing, identify the function whose graph has two zeros.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 81\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 8x + 16\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2+ 8x + 16\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 12x + 36\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2− 81\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Without graphing, identify the function whose graph has two zeros.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 10x + 25\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2+ 4x − 21\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2+16x + 64\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x) = x^2− 14x + 49\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = x^2+ 4x − 21\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the equation: \(x^2− 18x + 90 = 9\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x = -9\) </item>
  <item> \(x = -9\) and \(x=9\) </item>
  <item> \(x= -10\) and \(x=8\) </item>
  <item> \(x=9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=9\)</para></section>
